    "description": "<p><strong>\"How Should Health Researchers Advance Health Equity in Southeast Asia?\"</strong> workshop was held in Mahidol Oxford Tropical Medicine Research Unit (MORU) Bangkok on 23rd &ndash; 24th June 2026.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This workshop examined examine what equity and health equity mean in the Southeast Asian context; identify context-specific drivers of health inequity; and consider how health research priorities, questions and practices can be shaped to better address local needs.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Workshop Organisers</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Professor Phaik Yeong Cheah<br>Mahidol Oxford Tropical Medicine Research Unit (MORU) | Southeast Asia Bioethics Network (SEABioN) | Global Health Bioethics Network (GHBN)</li>\n<li>Associate Professor Sharon Kaur Gurmukh Singh<br>Universiti Malaya | Southeast Asia Bioethics Network (SEABioN) | Global Health Bioethics Network (GHBN)</li>\n<li>Professor Michael Parker<br>Ethox Centre, University of Oxford | Global Health Bioethics Network (GHBN)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Funding:</strong> Wellcome through MORU, SEABioN and GHBN</p>"
  },
