    "description_stripped": "\"How Should Health Researchers Advance Health Equity in Southeast Asia?\" workshop was held in Mahidol Oxford Tropical Medicine Research Unit (MORU) Bangkok on 23rd – 24th June 2026.\n\n \n\nThis workshop examined examine what equity and health equity mean in the Southeast Asian context; identify context-specific drivers of health inequity; and consider how health research priorities, questions and practices can be shaped to better address local needs.\n\n \n\nWorkshop Organisers\n\n\n\nProfessor Phaik Yeong CheahMahidol Oxford Tropical Medicine Research Unit (MORU) | Southeast Asia Bioethics Network (SEABioN) | Global Health Bioethics Network (GHBN)\n\nAssociate Professor Sharon Kaur Gurmukh SinghUniversiti Malaya | Southeast Asia Bioethics Network (SEABioN) | Global Health Bioethics Network (GHBN)\n\nProfessor Michael ParkerEthox Centre, University of Oxford | Global Health Bioethics Network (GHBN)\n\n\n \n\nFunding: Wellcome through MORU, SEABioN and GHBN",
